# The whole product proposition is that a parse-then-write round trip is
# byte-identical, so git must never rewrite a byte of anything it stores.
# `* text=auto` would convert tests/corpus/*.archimate to CRLF on a Windows
# clone and break the identity test in a way nobody would connect to git.
* -text

# The one exception: the installer has to run under `sh` after a Windows clone,
# and CRLF there fails with `$'\r': command not found`.
*.sh text eol=lf
